# Motion+ private registry (motion.dev/ui). Safe to commit: this references an
# environment variable, never the token itself.
#
# MOTION_TOKEN MUST BE SET ON EVERY MACHINE THAT RUNS `npm install`, AND THAT
# INCLUDES THE DEPLOY. It is not a local convenience — `motion-plus` is a real
# dependency resolved from this registry, so a build host without the token
# cannot install the tree at all. On this repo's own machines the token lives
# in ~/.npmrc and ~/.zshenv; there is no .env.local, and an earlier version of
# this comment sent people looking for one.
#
# READ THE STATUS CODE, IT TELLS YOU WHICH FAILURE IT IS. Measured against
# https://api.motion.dev/npm/@motionplus/core/-/core-2.12.0.tgz on 2026-08-21:
#
#   400 Bad Request   MOTION_TOKEN IS UNSET OR EMPTY in the environment. npm
#                     leaves `${MOTION_TOKEN}` unexpanded and sends it as the
#                     bearer verbatim; the registry rejects the malformed
#                     header. This is the Vercel failure — the fix is an
#                     environment variable on the project, not a new token.
#   401 Unauthorized  The token is present but wrong, revoked or expired.
#                     THIS is the one that needs a new token.
#   200               Good.
#
# So a deploy that dies on 400 has never seen the secret. Don't go regenerating
# one on the strength of a red build.
@motionplus:registry=https://api.motion.dev/npm/
//api.motion.dev/npm/:_authToken=${MOTION_TOKEN}
